My apologies, that was a classic API payload mismatch! 

The FastAPI backend was returning the object nested inside a `result` wrapper like this:
```json
{
  "message": "Photo processed successfully",
  "result": {
    "detected": [...],
    "unknown_count": 1
  }
}
```
But the frontend was trying to access `detected` directly from the top-level response! I have updated the frontend code to correctly parse `responseData.result` instead.

Since the frontend runs locally and hot-reloads instantly, you don't need to restart anything. Just **refresh the page** in your browser and try processing the image one more time!
